      "card_ids": ["C117","C105","C96","C92"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability records for lipophilic fused heteroaromatics are high: tryptanthrin Caco-2 Papp 22.5-61.38 ×10^-6 cm/s and concluded well absorbed, netupitant >20 ×10^-6, and 7c 24.3 ×10^-6; this supports absorption for the query's fused aromatic scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C96","C88","C97","C107","C124","C95"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility records are mostly low (telmisartan 0.09 µg/mL BCS II, camptothecin 2.5 µg/mL, toltrazuril 0.41 µg/mL, compound 1 0.3-4 µg/mL), but low solubility alone is not affirmative F<20% evidence; telmisartan is BCS II with dissolution-limited absorption yet is orally absorbed.",
      "card_ids": ["C105","C92","C112","C117","C91","C122"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 evidence is directionally mixed: high permeability records support absorption while low solubility records for other molecules caution against assuming high absorption; neither direction is query-specific or endpoint-determinative.",
      "card_ids": ["C96","C105","C92","C97"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C96","C88","C97","C99","C107","C124","C134","C95","C105","C92","C112","C117","C91","C122","C101","C135"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No query-specific solubility or permeability data; all L4 records concern other reference molecules.",
    "Query dose, formulation, and prandial state are unknown; food effects and solubility-limited absorption cannot be excluded.",
    "No query-specific first-pass metabolism, efflux, or clearance measurements.",
    "L4 low-solubility records are indirect and none establish F<20% for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L1/L2 direct human absolute BA values (43-91%) and L3 oral exposure records support F≥20%. L4 adds mixed absorption-component evidence: high permeability for lipophilic fused heteroaromatics supports absorption, while low solubility records for other molecules are indirect and not query-specific. No affirmative F<20% evidence exists, so the prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

